; RockCluster1 — Rock terrain visual (emits `rocks`), variant 1 of 6: the plain three-boulder
; read, no pebbles. The simplest tile in the set, and the closest in spirit to the original
; cluster this file replaced.
;
; 3x Rock_Medium_1 at 0.09735 + 8 grass tufts (the lowest tuft count in the set — this variant
; carries the most large-rock silhouette, so it needs the least ground dressing to stop the
; tile reading as bare).
;
; BUILT BY A ONE-OFF HEADLESS SCRIPT, NOT HAND-AUTHORED, AND NOT EDITABLE BY HAND — same
; generator, MultiMesh buffer layout and headless caveat as the grass-family pass; see
; GrassCommonShort.tscn's header. Re-run the generator to change anything below.
;
; INHERITS THE GRASS CALIBRATION BASELINE (human sign-off 2026-09-08): slab BoxMesh
; 1.0 x 0.2 x 1.0 at y=-0.1 (1.0 is the cross-tile seam-gap fix, do not narrow it), 2 blotchy
; floor patches at y=0.001, fixed-seed deterministic scatter within +/-0.42 tile-units of
; centre, +/-18% jitter, everything ground-level under one node named "Slab" (the
; OcclusionFader exemption convention). Slab keeps Rock's own grey Color(0.55, 0.55, 0.58).
;
; "SEVERAL SMALL ROCKS, NOT ONE GIANT ROCK" IS STILL THE RULING and is preserved exactly. All
; three MegaKit rock meshes target 0.220 tile-units — the SAME figure Scrub.tscn uses, so one
; mesh is never two sizes in the same world — which sits inside the established 0.19-0.25 band
; and far under the 0.877 natural height that drew the original human complaint. Variety comes
; from count and arrangement, not from resizing the same stone.
;
; GRASS TUFTS ARE DRESSING, NOT GRAZING COVER, and the numbers are what enforce that: scale
; 0.06 (raw AABB 1.334103 -> 0.080 tile-units) at 8-12 instances per tile, against Grass's own
; 0.075 at 36 and Wild grass's 0.065 at 32. They are the SHORTEST and SPARSEST grass anywhere
; in the project, deliberately. They exist because the MegaKit ships no mossy rock and moss was
; what tied the old rock tiles to the ground around them (human ruling 2026-09-08: replace moss
; with grass tufts at the rock bases). Rock emits `rocks` ALONE — blades here are no more a tag
; claim than Scrub's are, since `emitted_tags` is read from the .tres and never from a scene.
; IF THESE READ AS GRAZING LAND RATHER THAN AS DRESSING, THE COUNT IS THE DIAL TO TURN DOWN.
;
; GREY PALETTE ONLY (human ruling 2026-09-08). Every rock uses Rocks_Diffuse; the MegaKit's
; second, sand-coloured Rocks_Desert_Diffuse is deliberately unused. HONEST CAVEAT: the pebbles
; carry PathRocks_Diffuse, a separate MegaKit texture — same pack and same grey family, but not
; literally the same file. For a strict single-palette Rock, drop the pebbles and use only the
; three Rock_Medium meshes.
;
; Source: Stylized Nature MegaKit (Standard/free), Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — License.txt
; re-checked per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate. See
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_stylized_nature_megakit.tres.
;
; WHAT THIS PASS RETIRED FROM THE ROCK TERRAIN: `rock_1`, `rock_moss_2`, `rock_moss_5`
; (Ultimate Nature Pack) and `rock_2`, `rock_medium_moss`, `rocks_cluster` (Poly Pizza). Rock
; had been drawing from THREE packs at once — more than any other terrain — and is now
; single-pack. All six stay on disk unwired, not deleted (the disposition wild_grass.tres's
; Cactus/Palm and forest.tres's DeadTree/PineTree2 already have); `Rock1.tscn` and
; `test_rock_1_import.gd` still cover what the repo CONTAINS and are untouched. `Rock_Moss_3`
; is unaffected entirely — the Den prop keeps its own separate copy under assets/props/den/.
;
; GRASS COLOUR: TRUE GREEN BAND (2026-09-08, human-reported "the grass is very yellow").
; Grass.png is a 4-band vertical palette strip, each band 28px of a 512px texture, and the
; colour of every blade in this project comes from WHICH BAND its UVs land in — nothing tints
; anything (albedo is pure white, no vertex colours). The bands are:
;   band 1  x 0-27    rgb(177,152,0)  gold
;   band 2  x 28-55   rgb(57,149,0)   TRUE GREEN
;   band 3  x 56-83   rgb(185,87,0)   rust
;   band 4  x 84-111  rgb(103,163,0)  yellow-green
; Band 2 was the one band NOTHING in the project sampled: the Wispy meshes ship on band 1
; (gold) and the Common meshes on band 4 (yellow-green), which is why the world read warm.
; `uv1_offset` below re-centres this material's UV span in band 2, computed per mesh from its
; own measured span so every one lands with ~7px of margin on both band edges (mip bleed).
; The MESH IS UNTOUCHED — this is a material property and is reversible by deleting one line.
